1
00:00:00,392 --> 00:00:05,524
contexture-mcp connects agent hosts to application services.

2
00:00:05,958 --> 00:00:09,774
One model for application structure and agent interaction.

3
00:00:11,655 --> 00:00:14,655
MCP exposes tools for agents to call.

4
00:00:15,076 --> 00:00:20,405
As applications grow, flat tool lists become harder to navigate and maintain.

5
00:00:20,826 --> 00:00:24,800
What if agents could interact with capabilities the way object-oriented

6
00:00:24,813 --> 00:00:29,865
programs interact with objects—with a clear responsibility, guidance, and tools?

7
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:33,165
Explore its guidance.

8
00:00:33,589 --> 00:00:35,115
Then invoke its tools.

9
00:00:36,701 --> 00:00:41,977
Here is how Contexture implements that interaction, illustrated step by step.

10
00:00:42,372 --> 00:00:44,846
Discover reveals the starting points.

11
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:49,056
Inspect compares branches without loading their instructions.

12
00:00:49,451 --> 00:00:53,872
The agent opens Service Operations, then Incident Response.

13
00:00:54,293 --> 00:00:56,688
The selected branch reveals its guidance and

14
00:00:56,701 --> 00:01:00,938
tool definitions; unrelated details stay undisclosed.

15
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:05,780
The agent explicitly invokes read tools to check health and release history.

16
00:01:06,201 --> 00:01:10,714
Exploring a capability and executing business code remain separate.

17
00:01:11,109 --> 00:01:13,727
That is progressive context disclosure.

18
00:01:15,313 --> 00:01:19,379
This structure helps developers organize complex applications.

19
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:24,945
Each container combines a responsibility, local instructions, and members.

20
00:01:25,366 --> 00:01:27,642
Child containers build the hierarchy.

21
00:01:28,063 --> 00:01:33,089
Skills describe procedures; tools connect them to executable code.

22
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:36,353
Compose these objects into a gateway, and the

23
00:01:36,366 --> 00:01:39,260
agent can navigate the application by purpose.

24
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:43,353
Business services keep their own logic and authorization.

25
00:01:43,787 --> 00:01:46,550
One model connects how the agent explores

26
00:01:46,563 --> 00:01:48,405
with how the application is built.

27
00:01:50,013 --> 00:01:54,421
Build MCP servers that disclose what matters, when it matters.

28
00:01:54,842 --> 00:01:57,355
That's contexture-mcp.
